1
00:00:01,625 --> 00:00:03,000
Introduction.

2
00:00:04,375 --> 00:00:07,583
Radiation therapy to the head
and neck area involves

3
00:00:07,583 --> 00:00:12,166
some amount of radiation
that goes into the mucosal membranes.

4
00:00:12,166 --> 00:00:15,250
The mucosa are the membranes
that line your mouth and throat

5
00:00:15,625 --> 00:00:19,875
to produce saliva and fluids,
to allow you to eat and drink well.

6
00:00:20,125 --> 00:00:25,958
Unfortunately, radiation to these mucosal
areas leads to inflammation, sores,

7
00:00:25,958 --> 00:00:30,416
and pain in the mouth and throat,
which we call mucositis.

8
00:00:30,833 --> 00:00:35,041
Fortunately, we have a set of rinses
we would like you to do from the start

9
00:00:35,041 --> 00:00:40,250
of radiation to help lessen the amount
and degree of mucositis.

10
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:43,458
First and foremost,
we need you to take care

11
00:00:43,458 --> 00:00:46,541
of any dental procedures
prior to starting radiation.

12
00:00:46,958 --> 00:00:50,708
The reason is that
radiation will cause your teeth, gums,

13
00:00:50,708 --> 00:00:54,958
and jaw bones to take longer to heal
after any surgeries,

14
00:00:54,958 --> 00:00:59,541
root canals, fillings,
crowns, or procedures.

15
00:00:59,541 --> 00:01:03,500
We ask that if you have not had a dental
cleaning and dental X-rays

16
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:06,291
within the last six months,
to please make an appointment

17
00:01:06,291 --> 00:01:09,458
to see your dentist as soon as possible.

18
00:01:09,458 --> 00:01:15,000
If you do not have a dentist, we can
have you seen by our UCLA dentistry team.

19
00:01:15,666 --> 00:01:17,458
As for your dental hygiene,

20
00:01:17,458 --> 00:01:23,375
please use a soft toothbrush and continue
regular brushing during radiation.

21
00:01:23,375 --> 00:01:25,583
If toothpaste is irritating, it's

22
00:01:25,583 --> 00:01:28,666
okay to use just water when brushing.

23
00:01:28,666 --> 00:01:32,333
Be gentle in areas
that may become sensitive.

24
00:01:32,333 --> 00:01:36,541
If flossing is challenging,
you can stop flossing.
